1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,870
The disagreement began with a slight.

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:05,880
“You did not listen to me,” Maya said.

3
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:15,589
“You hear me, but you do not listen.” Lin was certainly tired, and he said something foolish about supervision.

4
00:00:15,589 --> 00:00:18,794
Everybody in the room went quiet.

5
00:00:18,794 --> 00:00:21,604
“Hello?” she said.

6
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:24,729
“Is anybody there?”

7
00:00:24,729 --> 00:00:32,923
She had a distinctive way of arguing: firstly the fact, then the feeling, then the request.

8
00:00:32,923 --> 00:00:42,018
“I owe you an apology,” he said, “and you owe me one.” She admired his honesty but not his timing.

9
00:00:42,018 --> 00:00:48,693
“That is undoubtedly true,” she said, “and utterly useless.”

10
00:00:48,693 --> 00:00:52,248
The real subject was the shape of the work.

11
00:00:52,248 --> 00:01:00,022
She wanted a mainstream project with a proper structure; he wanted a deliberate, slow one.

12
00:01:00,022 --> 00:01:04,807
“You cannot distinguish the two any more,” she said.

13
00:01:04,807 --> 00:01:15,446
“One of us has to be the beast.” A fisherman on the television talked about tides, and the sofa was covered in papers.

14
00:01:15,446 --> 00:01:19,726
They inspected the last three months like accountants.

15
00:01:19,726 --> 00:01:30,625
The parenting column, the letter from the preacher, a witty idiom, a tasty recipe: everything they had expended on pleasing other people.

16
00:01:30,625 --> 00:01:35,565
“This is a scar, not a strategy,” she said.

17
00:01:35,565 --> 00:01:38,200
“We are insuring a wreck.

18
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:45,489
And the word for it is attributive: we keep describing, and never deciding.”

19
00:01:45,489 --> 00:01:51,004
He was exhausted and, he admitted, easily distracted.

20
00:01:51,004 --> 00:01:55,504
“A figurative promise is worthless,” she said.

21
00:01:55,504 --> 00:02:07,603
“A priceless one costs something.” She spoke about sightseeing in an underdeveloped region and the way a town will beautify its front street while the back lanes flood.

22
00:02:07,603 --> 00:02:11,932
“A lick of paint is not a plan,” she said.

23
00:02:11,932 --> 00:02:15,547
Again and again he came back to one thing.

24
00:02:15,547 --> 00:02:18,667
“You are sure,” he said.

25
00:02:18,667 --> 00:02:20,297
“I am.

26
00:02:20,297 --> 00:02:23,622
Since March, definitely.

27
00:02:23,622 --> 00:02:49,430
And when I say it, I mean it literally — not as an excellent metaphor, not as a superb line, but as the plain fact that the work is ours.” “Any of it?” “All of it.” “Then it is invaluable,” he said, “and I will not lose it.” Clearly, one of them would have to dominate the schedule, though neither wanted to.

28
00:02:49,430 --> 00:03:04,780
An old man, a fisherman with a wooden boat, told them on the beach that a tide does not remain; whether you stay or go away is your own business, and the sea will never be more than the sea.
